  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task 2 result — supports in the SoV basis (exact zero tests; the tools cell and the supports cell above)\n\n| Phi | [2,1,0]: # support pairs of 64; slots per block (0,0),(0,1),(1,0),(1,1) | [3,1,0]: # support pairs of 225; slots per block |\n|---|---|---|\n| (a) generic pair g1 x g2; (b) random covectors; Omega_c[w] (x) Omega_c[w] and Omega_c[w'] (x) Omega_c[w']; Omega_c[w] (x) Omega_c[w'] and the reverse | **64 (full)**; 25, 15, 15, 9 | **225 (full)**; 81, 54, 54, 36 |\n| c1 (x) e1 (generic) and Omega_c[w] (x) e1 | 12; 3, 5, 1, 3 | 24; 6, 9, 3, 6 |\n| e1 (x) c2 (generic) and e1 (x) Omega_c[w'] | 35, 35; 8, 10, 10, 7 | 103, 101; 25, 28, 28, 22 (e1 x Omega_c[w']: 25, 27, 27, 22) |\n\n* Every Phi = c1 (x) c2 with both factors generic, and also the vacua Omega_c[w] (x) Omega_c[w'] (including w = w'), has the FULL support d2 = 64 / 225: all label pairs, every (c,c')-block fully \"populated\" (the numbers of slots equal the number of labels with the given pair of lone points). The x1-set as a function of x2 (and the x2-set as a function of x1) is the whole label set for every label: no dependence of the site-1 label set on c2 or x2 — the \"measure couples the two ladders\" statement of Part B in label language is the statement that the support is everything and all information sits in the coefficients (phi has full rank 8 / 15 as a d1 x d1 matrix; the vacuum Omega_c[w] (x) Omega_c[w] has rank 8 / 12, see Task 3).\n* One-site limits (must reproduce the one-site supports): c1 (x) e1 has only site-2 labels (lambda1|lambda1 c2) (12 / 24 states, all x2 in F2); e1 (x) c2 has the triangular support of Stage A: 35 / 103 states (15 / 29 with x1 in F1) — reproduced exactly.\n* The generic-pair support contains the union of the two one-site supports (35 / 103 states) and is strictly larger: 64 / 225 versus 35 / 103, and versus the pairs {x1 in F1} u {x2 in F2} (28 / 56). So the support is NOT the union of the one-site supports; it is everything.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 2b: the Yangian R-matrix of the reversed chain. Reversed monodromy Ttilde_ab(u) = sum_k L^(2)_ak(u - theta2) L^(1)_kb(u - theta1) (same lax code, factors swapped: Kronecker order site 1 (x) site 2, so Ttilde_ab = sum_k L1_kb (x) L2_ak). Solve R T_ab(u) = Ttilde_ab(u) R for all nine (a,b) at two rational u (exact). R commutes with the diagonal gl(3) (the u^1 coefficient), so it lies in the commutant of gl(3) on V (x) V; that commutant is generated here as the algebra spanned by words in 1, C12 = sum E1_ab E2_ba, D12 = sum E1_ab E1_bc E2_ca, D21 = sum E2_ab E2_bc E1_ca (closure; dimension tested against the number of highest-weight multiplicities squared), and the linear system is solved on its coefficients (Gram matrix of the flattened residuals, exact); the quartic invariants Q1 = sum E1_ab E2_bc E1_cd E2_da and Q2 = sum E1_ab E1_bc E2_cd E2_da are needed to separate multiplicity-2 irreps. *)\nlax2rev[x_] := lax2rev[x] = With[{L1 = lax1[1, x], L2 = lax1[2, x]}, Table[Sum[KroneckerProduct[L1[[k, j]], L2[[i, k]]], {k, 3}], {i, 3}, {j, 3}]];\nmono2rev[M_][x_] := mono2rev[M][x] = twistR[lax2rev[x], M];\nqminR[M_][rI_, cJ_][x_] := Sum[Signature[σ] Dot @@ Table[mono2rev[M][x - (k - 1) hN][[σ[[k]], cJ[[k]]]], {k, Length[cJ]}], {σ, Permutations[rI]}];\ntL2R[a_, x_, M_] := Sum[qminR[M][rows, rows][x], {rows, Subsets[Range[3], {a}]}];\nBopR[x_] := mono2rev[Id3][x][[1, 1]] . qminR[Id3][{1, 2}, {1, 2}][x + hN] + mono2rev[Id3][x][[2, 1]] . qminR[Id3][{1, 2}, {1, 3}][x + hN];\n(* the commutant: highest-weight multiplicities of V (x) V, and the algebra generated by the coupling invariants *)\nE12t = E1[1, 2] + E2[1, 2]; E23t = E1[2, 3] + E2[2, 3];\nhwMult = Association[Table[With[{sec = Flatten[Position[wtBasis, mu]]}, mu -> Length[NullSpace[Join[Normal[E12t[[All, sec]]], Normal[E23t[[All, sec]]]]]]], {mu, Union[wtBasis]}]];\ndimComm = Total[Select[Values[hwMult], # > 0 &]^2];\nC12 = Sum[E1[a, b] . E2[b, a], {a, 3}, {b, 3}];\nD12 = Sum[E1[a, b] . E1[b, c] . E2[c, a], {a, 3}, {b, 3}, {c, 3}];\nD21 = Sum[E2[a, b] . E2[b, c] . E1[c, a], {a, 3}, {b, 3}, {c, 3}];\nQ1 = Sum[E1[a, b] . E2[b, c] . E1[c, d] . E2[d, a], {a, 3}, {b, 3}, {c, 3}, {d, 3}];\nQ2 = Sum[E1[a, b] . E1[b, c] . E2[c, d] . E2[d, a], {a, 3}, {b, 3}, {c, 3}, {d, 3}];\nflatS[W_] := ArrayReshape[W, {d2^2}];\ngramOf[L_] := Table[flatS[L[[i]]] . flatS[L[[j]]], {i, Length[L]}, {j, Length[L]}];\nindep[basis_, W_] := MatrixRank[gramOf[Append[basis, W]]] > Length[basis];\n{tims[\"commutant closure\"], commB} = AbsoluteTiming[Module[{bas = {id2}, gens = {C12, D12, D21, Q1, Q2}, frontier, new, W, iter = 0},\n   frontier = {id2};\n   While[Length[bas] < dimComm && frontier =!= {} && iter < 8, iter++; new = {};\n    Do[W = SparseArray[f . g]; If[indep[bas, W], AppendTo[bas, W]; AppendTo[new, W]], {f, frontier}, {g, gens}];\n    frontier = new];\n   bas]];\nchecks[\"commutant: dimension of the generated algebra vs sum of squared HW multiplicities\"] = {Length[commB], dimComm};\nchecks[\"commutant elements commute with the diagonal gl(3) (exact), all generators E_ij^tot\"] = And @@ Flatten[Table[zeroM[W . (E1[i, j] + E2[i, j]) - (E1[i, j] + E2[i, j]) . W], {W, commB}, {i, 3}, {j, 3}]];\nuR = {3/11, 2/9};\nresOf[W_] := Flatten[Table[flatS[W . lax2[u0][[a, b]] - lax2rev[u0][[a, b]] . W], {u0, uR}, {a, 3}, {b, 3}], 2];\n{tims[\"R: linear system on the commutant\"], nsR} = AbsoluteTiming[Module[{res = resOf /@ commB, Gm}, Gm = Table[Sum[res[[i, t]] . res[[j, t]], {t, Length[res[[1]]]}], {i, Length[commB]}, {j, Length[commB]}]; NullSpace[Gm]]];\nchecks[\"R: dimension of the solution space R T_ab = Ttilde_ab R (all a, b, two u)\"] = Length[nsR];\nRraw = SparseArray[Sum[nsR[[1, i]] commB[[i]], {i, Length[commB]}]];\nx0R = x0C . Rraw; scaleR = x0R[[First[Flatten[Position[x0C, 1]]]]];\nchecks[\"R: (e1 (x) e1) R proportional to e1 (x) e1 (exact)\"] = zeroM[SparseArray[x0R - scaleR x0C]];\nRm = SparseArray[Rraw/scaleR];   (* normalised: x0 R = x0 *)\n{tims[\"R: inverse\"], Rinv} = AbsoluteTiming[Module[{Af = Table[flatS[Rm . W], {W, commB}], bv = flatS[id2], dsol},\n   dsol = LinearSolve[Table[Af[[i]] . Af[[j]], {i, Length[commB]}, {j, Length[commB]}], Table[Af[[i]] . bv, {i, Length[commB]}]];\n   SparseArray[Sum[dsol[[k]] commB[[k]], {k, Length[commB]}]]]];\nchecks[\"R: R Rinv = 1 (exact), nonsingular\"] = zeroM[Rm . Rinv - id2];\nchecks[\"R: max denominator digits of R, Rinv; # nonzero entries\"] = {Max[IntegerLength /@ Denominator[Rm[\"NonzeroValues\"]]], Max[IntegerLength /@ Denominator[Rinv[\"NonzeroValues\"]]], {Length[Rm[\"NonzeroValues\"]], Length[Rinv[\"NonzeroValues\"]]}};\n(* checks on all nine entries at a third u, fusion t_a with the diagonal twist, and the SoV operator B *)\nu3 = 19/23;\nchecks[\"R: R T_ab = Ttilde_ab R at a third u = 19/23 (exact, all nine)\"] = And @@ Flatten[Table[zeroM[Rm . lax2[u3][[a, b]] - lax2rev[u3][[a, b]] . Rm], {a, 3}, {b, 3}]];\nchecks[\"R: ttilde_a(u) R = R t_a(u), twist diag(z), a = 1,2,3, u = 19/23 (exact)\"] = Table[zeroM[tL2R[a, u3, Zd] . Rm - Rm . tL2[a, u3, Zd]], {a, 3}];\nchecks[\"R: Btilde(u) R = R B(u) (untwisted SoV operator, exact, u = 19/23)\"] = zeroM[BopR[u3] . Rm - Rm . Bop2[u3]];\ngTest = nexp[(1/3) Ee[1, 2]] . nexp[-2 Ee[2, 3]] . nexp[(3/2) Ee[2, 1]] . nexp[(5/7) Ee[3, 1]];\ngg2 = SparseArray[KroneckerProduct[gTest, gTest]];\nchecks[\"R: R (rho(g) (x) rho(g)) = (rho(g) (x) rho(g)) R, rational g (exact)\"] = zeroM[Rm . gg2 - gg2 . Rm];\nGrid[{{\"commutant dim (generated), sum of squared HW multiplicities\", checks[\"commutant: dimension of the generated algebra vs sum of squared HW multiplicities\"]}, {\"commutant commutes with E_ij^tot\", checks[\"commutant elements commute with the diagonal gl(3) (exact), all generators E_ij^tot\"]}, {\"dim of {R : R T_ab = Ttilde_ab R} (expect 1)\", checks[\"R: dimension of the solution space R T_ab = Ttilde_ab R (all a, b, two u)\"]}, {\"(e1 (x) e1) R = e1 (x) e1 (after normalisation)\", checks[\"R: (e1 (x) e1) R proportional to e1 (x) e1 (exact)\"]}, {\"R Rinv = 1\", checks[\"R: R Rinv = 1 (exact), nonsingular\"]}, {\"max denominator digits R, Rinv; # nonzero R, Rinv (of d2^2)\", {checks[\"R: max denominator digits of R, Rinv; # nonzero entries\"], d2^2}}, {\"R T_ab = Ttilde_ab R at u = 19/23 (nine entries)\", checks[\"R: R T_ab = Ttilde_ab R at a third u = 19/23 (exact, all nine)\"]}, {\"ttilde_a R = R t_a (a = 1,2,3)\", checks[\"R: ttilde_a(u) R = R t_a(u), twist diag(z), a = 1,2,3, u = 19/23 (exact)\"]}, {\"Btilde R = R B\", checks[\"R: Btilde(u) R = R B(u) (untwisted SoV operator, exact, u = 19/23)\"]}, {\"R commutes with rho(g) (x) rho(g)\", checks[\"R: R (rho(g) (x) rho(g)) = (rho(g) (x) rho(g)) R, rational g (exact)\"]}, {\"times (s): commutant closure, linear system, inverse (solved inside the commutant)\", {tims[\"commutant closure\"], tims[\"R: linear system on the commutant\"], tims[\"R: inverse\"]}}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
