   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task 2b result — the R-matrix dressing (the three cells above): the reading of the site asymmetry is CONFIRMED\n\n**R-matrix** (cell 'Yangian R-matrix'): R T_ab(u) = Ttilde_ab(u) R for all nine (a,b), Ttilde(u) = L^(2)(u-theta2) L^(1)(u-theta1), as matrices on kets (so Psitilde = R Psi, Btilde = R B R^-1, <xtilde| = <x| R^-1). Solved exactly inside the commutant of the diagonal gl(3): the algebra generated by 1, C12 = sum E1_ab E2_ba, D12, D21 (cubic couplings) and the quartic couplings Q1, Q2 has dimension 8 resp. 14 = sum of squared highest-weight multiplicities of V (x) V (checked), and every element commutes with all E_ij^tot; the Gram matrix of the flattened residuals at two u (3/11, 2/9) has a **1-dimensional null space for both reps** (the quartic invariants are needed: words in 1, C12, D12, D21 alone give only 6 of 8 for the adjoint).\n\n| check (exact) | [2,1,0] | [3,1,0] |\n|---|---|---|\n| dim of the solution space | **1** | **1** |\n| R T_ab = Ttilde_ab R at a third u = 19/23 (all nine entries) | True | True |\n| ttilde_a(u) R = R t_a(u), twist diag(z), a = 1,2,3, u = 19/23 | True, True, True | True, True, True |\n| Btilde(u) R = R B(u) (the SoV operator) | True | True |\n| R commutes with rho(g) (x) rho(g), rational g | True | True |\n| (e1 (x) e1) R = e1 (x) e1 after normalising R | True | True |\n| R Rinv = 1 (Rinv solved inside the commutant) | True | True |\n| # nonzero entries of R, Rinv (of d2^2); max denominator digits R, Rinv | 322, 322 (of 4096); 7, 5 | 2285, 2285 (of 50625); 10, 7 |\n| R -> 1 as theta12 -> infinity (max \\|R - 1\\|; base t = 62/35 / theta2 = -100, t = 1404/7; driver) | 0.86 / 0.020 | 1.02 / 0.044 |\n| times (s): commutant closure, linear system, inverse | 0.08, 0.18, 0.01 | 3.1, 3.5, 0.33 |\n\n**Dressed test** (cells 'dressed' and 'locus'): the correct side is **Phi = (e1 (x) c2(g2)) . R** (row vector times R):\n\n| | [2,1,0] | [3,1,0] |\n|---|---|---|\n| (e1 (x) c2) R: # support pairs; all with x1 in F1 = {(lambda1\\|lambda1 c1)}? # distinct x1, x2 | **12 of 64; True**; 2, 8 | **24 of 225; True**; 2, 15 |\n| per-label automatic count (ladder-2 brackets, ladder-1 factor a scalar): generic g2 / g2 = Omega_c[w'] | **5 / 5** | **7 / 5** |\n| the same for the undressed e1 (x) c2 (Stage A) | 17 | 40 |\n| (e1 (x) c2) R^-1 (wrong side): support, count | 36 pairs, 17 | 106 pairs, 41 |\n| control: (c1 (x) e1) R (dressing the cheap site-1 rotation): support; counts (site-1 brackets, site-2 brackets) | 35 pairs; 17, 17 | 103 pairs; 40, 41 |\n\nSo the R-dressed site-2 rotation has the SITE-1 structure: support only on the site-1 labels (lambda1|lambda1 c1) (factors v3(theta1 - c1 h)/v3(theta1 - lambda2 h)), count 5 / 7, and the mirror dressing undoes the cheapness of a site-1 rotation (control: 17 / 40). The site asymmetry of Stage A is exactly the R-matrix conjugation theta12 -> -theta12.\n\n**Loci of the dressed covector in g2 (Gauss chart, symbolic):**\n* [2,1,0]: only the column (x1 = (2|20), c' = 0) is non-automatic; its Pfaffian = const x gB^2 x (167 gA^2 - 264 (gB + gA gC)). The conic constant is **cc = 167/264 = cc1(-t) = (t+3)/(2(t+2)) at t = 62/35** (this is the exact value; the spec's 229/342 does not equal (t+3)/(2(t+2)) at t = 62/35 — it is not matched by any shift tested, the structural statement 'cc1(t -> -t)' is what is confirmed). Count on the conic: **4** (generic 5; the point (4, 16 cc - 20, 5)); also the locus gB = 0. Checked at three more (h,theta) points in the driver: cc = 37/59 at (1/3,(1/5,-4/9)), 61/94 at (1/2,(3/7,-1/4)) — both = (t+3)/(2(t+2)); and 1425/2836 at theta2 = -100.\n* [3,1,0]: conic-type factors with constants {1, 404/501, 167/264, 3371/7348, 101/66}; **cc = 1, the vacuum family beta + alpha gamma = alpha^2, is among them and gives the count 5** (generic 7; the other conics 7, 6); other factors: gB, a non-conic quartic, ... The best locus is the vacuum family with count 5 — as expected (the mirror image of the site-1 result, where the [3,1,0] best locus is the one-site vacuum family). The constant 167/264 = (t+3)/(2(t+2)) also appears at t = 62/35 (count 7, not reducing).",
