  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task 3 result — block ranks and bracket-product counts (the two cells above)\n\nFormat per block (c,c') in the order (0,0), (0,1), (1,0), (1,1): r = matrix rank (exact lower bound on the number of bracket products in the block), P = upper bound of the pivot decomposition (smaller of the two orientations; the orientation sums are in the printed cell). Every identity (phi-form and block form with explicit bracket products, all states) holds at 1e-39 or better (printed). nMin = 6 ([2,1,0]) / 10 ([3,1,0]) is the block size, 4 blocks.\n\n**[2,1,0]** (dim V^2 = 64):\n\n| Phi | slots | r per block | sum r | P per block | **sum P** |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| (a) generic pair g1 x g2 | 25,15,15,9 | 5,3,3,3 | 14 | 10,5,5,3 | **23** |\n| (b) random covectors (control) | same | 5,3,3,3 | 14 | 10,5,5,3 | 23 |\n| (c) Omega_c[w] x Omega_c[w] (= Omega_c[w'] x Omega_c[w'], same numbers) | same | 5,3,3,2 | 13 | 10,3,3,2 | **18** |\n| (d) Omega_c[w] x Omega_c[w'] and Omega_c[w'] x Omega_c[w] | same | 5,3,3,2 | 13 | 10,5,5,2 | **22** |\n| (e) Omega_c[w] x e1 (blocks all rank 1) | 3,5,1,3 | 1,1,1,1 | 4 | 1,2,1,1 | 5 (= one-site generic; Omega_c is not on the adjoint's best locus) |\n| (e') e1 x Omega_c[w'] | 8,10,10,7 | 3,3,3,2 | 11 | 5,4,4,2 | 15 (Stage A block form: 11 / 15) |\n| (f) c1(g1) x e1 | 3,5,1,3 | 1,1,1,1 | 4 | 1,2,1,1 | 5 |\n| (f') e1 x c2(g2) | 8,10,10,7 | 3,3,3,2 | 11 | 5,4,4,2 | 15 |\n| (e3) c1(site-1 quadric point (4,23,5)) x e1 | | 1,1,1,1 | 4 | 1,1,1,1 | **4** |\n| (g) (e1 x Omega_c[w']) R (R-dressed vacuum) | 3,1,5,3 | 1,1,1,1 | 4 | 1,1,2,1 | **5** |\n| (g2) (e1 x c2(dressed conic point)) R | | 1,1,1,1 | 4 | | **4** |\n| (g3) (e1 x c2(generic)) R | | | 4 | | 5 |\n| (h1) (e1 x Omega_c[w']) R (rho(g1) x 1), g1 = Gauss parameters of Omega_c[w] | 25,15,15,9 | 5,3,3,3 | 14 | 10,5,5,3 | **23** |\n| (h2) (Omega_c[w] x e1) R (1 x rho(g2)), g2 = Omega_c[w'] | same | 5,3,3,3 | 14 | 10,5,5,3 | **23** |\n| (h3) (e1 x c2(g2)) R (rho(g1) x 1), generic g1, g2 | same | 5,3,3,3 | 14 | | 23 |\n\n**[3,1,0]** (dim V^2 = 225):\n\n| Phi | slots | r per block | sum r | P per block | **sum P** |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| (a) generic pair | 81,54,54,36 | 9,6,6,6 | 27 | 18,12,12,12 | **54** |\n| (b) random covectors | same | 9,6,6,6 | 27 | 18,12,12,12 | 54 |\n| (c) Omega_c[w] x Omega_c[w] (= w' case) | same | 8,6,6,6 | 26 | 22,6,6,6 | **40** |\n| (d) Omega_c[w] x Omega_c[w'] and reverse | same | 9,6,6,6 | 27 | 18,12,12,12 | **54** (= generic) |\n| (e) Omega_c[w] x e1 (the one-site vacuum-family best locus) | 6,9,3,6 | 1,1,1,1 | 4 | 1,2,1,1 | **5** |\n| (e') e1 x Omega_c[w'] | 25,27,27,22 | 6,6,6,4 | 22 | 10,9,9,7 | 35 |\n| (f) c1(g1) x e1 generic | 6,9,3,6 | 1,1,1,1 | 4 | 2,2,1,2 | 7 |\n| (f') e1 x c2(g2) generic | 25,28,28,22 | 6,6,6,4 | 22 | 10,9,9,7 | 35 (Stage A block form: 22 / 35) |\n| (g) (e1 x Omega_c[w']) R | 6,3,9,6 | 1,1,1,1 | 4 | 1,1,2,1 | **5** |\n| (g3) (e1 x c2(generic)) R | | 1,1,1,1 | 4 | 2,1,2,2 | 7 |\n| (h1), (h2), (h3) (R-dressed two-rotation candidates) | 81,54,54,36 | 9,6,6,6 | 27 | 18,12,12,12 | **54** |\n\n**Regression (e)/(f), blocks with site 2 = e1**: every block has rank <= 1 (a single site-2 slot (the vacuum minor of ladder 2) times a ladder-1 2-form) and **P(c,c') = (rank of column c of the one-site tensor of the group c2 = c')/2**, i.e. the block count is exactly the one-site automatic column count; checked for Omega_c[w] x e1 and generic c1 x e1 against the one-site tensors rebuilt from Kg: True, True. (All four (c,c') blocks are populated, not only c' = lambda2 as one might have expected: slots 3,5,1,3 resp. 6,9,3,6 for Omega_c[w] x e1, because the site-2 labels (lambda1|lambda1 c2) occur for every c2 = 0..lambda2 with the factors lambda2^(c2).) Totals 5 / 5 resp. 5 / 7 = the one-site generic and vacuum-family counts of the general notebook (adjoint 5 generic; [3,1,0] 7 generic, 5 on the vacuum family). For e1 x c2 the block ranks and counts are Stage A's (cell 19 of the Stage A notebook: ranks 3,3,3,2 / 6,6,6,4, sums 11 / 22, products 15 / 35).\n\n**det6 regression (essential, plan section 7).** The vacuum is a single det6; its Laplace expansion along the three ladder-1 rows has Binomial[6,3] = 20 terms, each a product of a 3x3 ladder-1 and a complementary 3x3 ladder-2 bracket minor. Every 3x3 minor is a combination over the lone point c of (2-form)_c v3(theta - c h), and the same Laplace term feeds all four (c,c') blocks, so each block has r_cc' <= 20 and (the terms being summed over (c,c')) the sum of r over the 4 blocks is bounded by 80 — NOT by 20. The per-block bound is not binding because nMin = 6 / 10 < 20: the Laplace structure cannot be seen in the matrix ranks alone. What IS visible, and passes: **the vacuum has strictly lower ranks and much lower counts than the generic pair**: [2,1,0] sum r 13 vs 14 (block (1,1): 2 vs 3), sum P 18 vs 23; [3,1,0] sum r 26 vs 27 (block (0,0): 8 vs 9), sum P 40 vs 54; and the d1 x d1 coefficient matrix phi has rank 8 (= full; same as generic) for [2,1,0] but **12 < 15 for [3,1,0]** (vacuum, both w and w') against 15 for the generic pair and for Omega_c[w] x Omega_c[w']. So the bookkeeping (signs of the minors, the lone-point convention on site 2, the K normalisation) is right: the overlap identity holds with explicit bracket products at 1e-39 or better for every Phi. The optional termwise comparison of the 20 Laplace terms with A^(c,c') was NOT done: the per-ladder 3x3 minors are trilinear forms in (Q3, Q2, Q3) that are not polynomials in our monomials (minor x Q3) without the Baxter / Plucker relations of the eigenstates, so a termwise comparison is not meaningful as a polynomial identity (it would need the relations); the state-by-state identity is the check that was done.\n\n**First decisive number (plan section 6).** One-site block counts: site 1: 5 generic / 4 (adjoint quadric) / 5 ([3,1,0] vacuum family), 7 generic ([3,1,0]); site 2 DRESSED (the mirror image): 5 / 4 resp. 7 / 5; site 2 undressed: 15 / 35. The 'product of one-site counts': generic site 1 x generic dressed site 2 = 25 ([2,1,0]), 49 ([3,1,0]); best x best = 4 x 4 = 16, 5 x 5 = 25; (Omega_c[w] x e1) x undressed (e1 x Omega_c[w']) = 75, 175. **The count of (d) Omega_c[w] x Omega_c[w'] is 22 ([2,1,0]) and 54 ([3,1,0]): for [2,1,0] it lies just below the generic pair (23) and the generic product (25), far above the best-x-best product 16; for [3,1,0] it is EXACTLY the generic pair's count (ranks and counts identical, 54), above every product (49, 25, 175 vs 54: only the undressed product is higher).** The vacuum w = w' is cheaper (18 / 40) but still far above the products. So two different vacua do NOT decouple at the bracket level; the dressing by R does not make a two-rotation covector cheap either ((h1)-(h3) are exactly generic: the R-dressed candidates (e1 x Omega_c[w']) R (rho(g1) x 1) and (Omega_c[w] x e1) R (1 x rho(g2)) cost 23 / 54).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 4: the family Omega_c[w] (x) Omega_c[w'] over (w1, w2, w1', w2'). Coordinates alpha = 1/w1, s = 1/w2 (a1, s1 for w; a2, s2 for w'): Omega_c = gaussCov[{a, -a s, a + s}] is a polynomial vector, so the blocks A^(c,c')(a1,s1,a2,s2) are matrices of POLYNOMIALS (no denominators to clear): phi_m = sum over the nonzero entries of Kt of K c1_nu1 c2_nu2. *)\nc1S = Expand /@ Normal[gaussVac[{a1, s1}]]; c2S = Expand /@ Normal[gaussVac[{a2, s2}]];\nnzPos = Kt[\"NonzeroPositions\"]; nzVal = Kt[\"NonzeroValues\"];\nphiSym[c1_, c2_] := Module[{v = ConstantArray[0, d2], nu, m, n1, n2}, Do[nu = nzPos[[k, 1]]; m = nzPos[[k, 2]]; n1 = Quotient[nu - 1, d1] + 1; n2 = Mod[nu - 1, d1] + 1; v[[m]] += nzVal[[k]] c1[[n1]] c2[[n2]], {k, Length[nzPos]}]; ArrayReshape[Map[Expand, v][[Flatten[mIdxMat]]], {d1, d1}]];\n{tims[\"family: symbolic phi\"], phFam} = AbsoluteTiming[phiSym[c1S, c2S]];\nbgFam = blockOf[phFam];\nfamVars = {a1, s1, a2, s2};\nchecks[\"family: symbolic phi at a rational point equals the numeric phi of Omega_c[w] (x) Omega_c[w'] (exact)\"] = (phFam /. Thread[famVars -> {1/wN[[1]], 1/wN[[2]], 1/wP[[1]], 1/wP[[2]]}]) === phiMat[kron[Ωc[wN], Ωc[wP]]];\nchecks[\"family: degrees of the block entries (max total degree), # terms (max)\"] = {Max[Exponent[#, famVars] & /@ Flatten[phFam]] // Max, Max[Length[Expand[#]] & /@ Flatten[phFam] /. Plus -> List]};\nSeedRandom[41];\nrandPt[] := Thread[famVars -> RandomChoice[{-3, -2, -3/2, -1, -1/2, 1/2, 1, 3/2, 2, 3, 5/2, 4}, 4]];\nrkAtPt[pt_] := Table[MatrixRank[bgFam[k] /. pt], {k, Keys[bgFam]}];\n{tims[\"family: generic ranks (3 points)\"], rkGenFam} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[rkAtPt[randPt[]], {3}]];\nchecks[\"family: generic block ranks r_cc' (max over 3 random points), blocks (0,0),(0,1),(1,0),(1,1) in key order\"] = Max /@ Transpose[rkGenFam];\nGrid[{{\"symbolic phi at (a1,s1,a2,s2) = (1/w1, 1/w2, 1/w1', 1/w2') equals the numeric phi\", checks[\"family: symbolic phi at a rational point equals the numeric phi of Omega_c[w] (x) Omega_c[w'] (exact)\"]}, {\"max total degree per variable in phi; max # terms of an entry\", checks[\"family: degrees of the block entries (max total degree), # terms (max)\"]}, {\"block keys\", Keys[bgFam]}, {\"generic ranks at 3 random points\", rkGenFam}, {\"generic ranks (max)\", checks[\"family: generic block ranks r_cc' (max over 3 random points), blocks (0,0),(0,1),(1,0),(1,1) in key order\"]}, {\"times (s): symbolic phi, generic ranks\", {tims[\"family: symbolic phi\"], tims[\"family: generic ranks (3 points)\"]}}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
