   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task 4b result — the (infinity, infinity) family with w1 != w1' (the cell above)\n\nPhi = gaussCov[{a,0,a}] (x) gaussCov[{a',0,a'}], a = 1/w1, a' = 1/w1'. Limit confirmed: Omega_c = gaussCov[{a, -a s, a+s}] at s = 0 is gaussCov[{a,0,a}] symbolically (exact), and numerically Omega_c[{3/2, 10^6}] differs from gaussCov[{2/3,0,2/3}] by 1e-6 relative. Blocks in the order (0,0),(0,1),(1,0),(1,1). All three pairs (2/3,-5/7), (3/2,1/4), (-4/5,7/3) give identical numbers. Overlap identity at (2/3,-5/7): phi-form 1e-44 / 1e-40 and block form with explicit bracket products (12 / 45 products) 1e-44 / 1e-39 ([2,1,0] / [3,1,0]).\n\n| case | [2,1,0] slots | r | P (min orient.) | P=r? | sum r / **sum P** | [3,1,0] slots | r | P | P=r? | sum r / **sum P** |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **(inf,inf), a != a' (3 points)** | 11,11,9,9 | 3,3,2,2 | 4,4,2,2 | F,F,T,T | 10 / **12** | 45,45,36,36 | 6,6,6,6 | 12,12,9,12 | F,F,F,F | 24 / **45** |\n| gaussCov[{a,0,a}] x Om_c[w'] | 21,15,15,9 | 5,3,3,2 | 8,5,5,2 | F,F,F,T | 13 / 20 | 72,54,54,36 | 9,6,6,6 | 18,12,12,12 | all F | 27 / 54 |\n| Om_c[w] x gaussCov[{a',0,a'}] | 15,15,9,9 | 3,3,2,2 | 5,5,2,2 | F,F,T,T | 10 / 14 | 54,54,36,36 | 6,6,6,6 | 12,12,9,12 | all F | 24 / 45 |\n| vacuum Om_c[w] x Om_c[w] | 25,15,15,9 | 5,3,3,2 | 10,3,3,2 | F,T,T,T | 13 / 18 | 81,54,54,36 | 8,6,6,6 | 22,6,6,6 | F,T,T,T | 26 / 40 |\n| generic pair | 25,15,15,9 | 5,3,3,3 | 10,5,5,3 | F,F,F,T | 14 / 23 | 81,54,54,36 | 9,6,6,6 | 18,12,12,12 | all F | 27 / 54 |\n| global rotation a = a' (8/14 line) | 4,6,6,9 | 2,2,2,2 | 2,2,2,2 | all T | 8 / 8 | 9,18,18,36 | 2,3,3,6 | 2,3,3,6 | all T | 14 / 14 |\n\n(P rows / cols orientation sums: [2,1,0] (4,4,2,2)/(5,5,2,2); [3,1,0] (12,12,9,12)/(24,24,12,12).)\n\n**Plane (a, a') symbolic.** Generic ranks (3 random points): (3,3,2,2) / (6,6,6,6). Rank-drop hypersurface components (common factors of det(PAQ)): [2,1,0]: (0,0): none found; (0,1): a, a-a', a'; (1,0): a'; (1,1): a'. [3,1,0]: (0,0): a, a-a', a'; (0,1): a, a-a', a'; (1,0): a, a', a-a', 31a-66a', 66a-31a', 53a-22a', and a quartic; (1,1): a, a', 9a-44a', 6a-19a', 2134a^2-1188aa'+279a'^2, and a quartic (t-dependent ratio lines, as in Task 4). Note for [2,1,0] the drop of block (0,0) from 3 to 2 on a = a' is visible in the line table but was not detected by the common-factor method (the method is only a hypersurface heuristic). Sum P on lines (2 members each): a = a': 8 / 14; a = 0: 8 / 19; a' = 0: 4 / 4 (trivial, one factor = e1); generic a != a': 12 / 45.\n\n**Verdict.** For [3,1,0] the (inf,inf) family with w1 != w1' costs **sum P = 45 against 54 (generic) and 40 (vacuum)**; lower bound sum r = 24, no block has P = r. It is NOT cheap (threshold ~25 not met), so no wedge decomposition was listed for [3,1,0]. For [2,1,0] it costs **12 against 23 (generic) and 18 (vacuum)**, lower bound 10; blocks (1,0) and (1,1) have P = r = 2; the explicit wedge decomposition at (a,a') = (2/3,-5/7) is printed in the cell above (block (0,0): 3 terms, ladder-1 wedges 2+1+1, ladder-2 one wedge each; (0,1): same; (1,0): 2 terms; (1,1): 2 terms; F, G over m = -3..0). The cheap global-rotation line a = a' (8 / 14) is the only exact one but is a global rotation, not the family of interest.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
