   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task 5 result — one-site-fixed slices (the two cells above)\n\n**(A) site 2 fixed at Omega_c[w'], site 1 free g1 = (gA,gB,gC)** — the blocks are polynomial matrices in 3 variables (symbolic phi checked against the numeric one; exact). Generic ranks: [2,1,0] 5,3,3,2 (note: the (1,1) block already has the vacuum value 2 for EVERY g1, because site 2 is a vacuum), [3,1,0] 9,6,6,6. Rank-drop hypersurfaces: [2,1,0] only block (0,0): one irreducible hypersurface of degree 12 (167 terms); the other blocks have none. [3,1,0]: block (1,1): gA, 63 gA - 176, 52283 gA^2 - 16632 gA + 2232, a quadric-type factor 22698 gA^2 - 10325 gA - 9300 - 7998 (gB + gA gC), and a degree-4 factor; block (0,0): high-degree factor (line section only); (0,1), (1,0): none.\n\nCounts sum P at 3 members of each locus (ranks never change on these loci except where stated):\n\n| locus (site 1, with site 2 = Omega_c[w']) | [2,1,0] | [3,1,0] |\n|---|---|---|\n| generic g1 | 22 | 54 |\n| vacuum family beta + alpha gamma = alpha^2 | 22 | 54 |\n| b3 = beta + alpha gamma = 0 | 22 | 54 |\n| conics cc1(t) (the adjoint site-1 quadric), cc1(-t) (dressed), cc1(1-t) (undressed site 2) | 22, 22, 22 | 54, 54, 54 |\n| beta = 0 | 20 | 54 |\n| alpha = alpha' (common w1; surface) | 20 | 49 |\n| alpha = alpha' and the vacuum family | **18** (= common-w1 count of Task 4) | **40** (r(0,0) = 8) |\n| alpha = alpha', beta = 0 | 18 | 48 |\n\n**Answer to the plan question (A):** the one-site loci of the site-1 problem — the vacuum family beta + alpha gamma = alpha^2 (the [3,1,0] best locus) and, for the adjoint, the quadric 2(t-2)(beta + alpha gamma) = (t-3) alpha^2 — do NOT appear as count-reducing loci when site 2 is Omega_c[w']: counts 22 / 54 on them, the same as for generic g1 (the reduction 23 -> 22 relative to the generic pair is entirely due to the fixed vacuum on site 2, not to g1). The reducing loci of g1 are cross loci that depend on w': alpha = 1/w1 = alpha' (common w1) [20 / 49; with the vacuum condition 18 / 40] and beta = 0 [20 / 54]. So the two sites do NOT decouple at the bracket level; the cross terms appear exactly as loci depending on w' (alpha = alpha'). Best count at fixed g2 (among the loci tested): **18 ([2,1,0]) / 40 ([3,1,0])**.\n\n**(B) site 1 fixed at Omega_c[w], site 2 free g2 = (gA,gB,gC).** Generic ranks 5,3,3,3 / 9,6,6,6. Rank-drop hypersurfaces: [2,1,0]: block (0,0): gB and a degree-13 hypersurface (147 terms); **block (1,1): gA, -4 + 25 gB + 10 gC, and gA^2 - gB - gA gC, i.e. exactly the vacuum family beta + alpha gamma = alpha^2 of site 2** (rank 3 -> 2 there); (0,1), (1,0): none. [3,1,0]: block (1,1): gA, a bilinear factor (-168 gA + 1144 gB + 465 gA gB + 1330 gA gC), degree 7 and degree 9 factors; (0,0): line section only.\n\n| locus (site 2, with site 1 = Omega_c[w]) | [2,1,0] | [3,1,0] |\n|---|---|---|\n| generic g2 | 23 | 54 |\n| vacuum family (b3 = alpha^2) | 22 (block (1,1) rank 2) | 54 |\n| b3 = 0 | 22 | 50 |\n| conics cc1(t), cc1(-t), cc1(1-t) | 23, 23, 23 | 54, 54, 54 |\n| **beta = 0** | **16** (ranks 3,3,3,3, sum r 12) | 48 (ranks 6,6,6,6) |\n| alpha = alpha_w (w1' = w1, surface) | 23 | 54 |\n| alpha = alpha_w and vacuum family | 18 | 40 |\n| alpha = alpha_w, beta = 0 | 16 | 48 |\n\n(B) is not the mirror of (A): the site-2 vacuum family is a genuine rank-drop locus (block (1,1)) and beta = 0 on site 2 is the cheapest line (16 for the adjoint, i.e. the number 4 x 4 of the best x best product, but NOT CG-complete-tested). Best count at fixed g1: **16 / 40**.\n\n**Type-pair scan (6-parameter family, simple loci per site; the second cell above):** minimum sum P over ordered pairs of site types {generic, vacuum, beta = 0, gamma = 0, alpha = 0, b3 = 0, three conics}: **[2,1,0]: 14** at (beta1 = 0, beta2 = 0) and (alpha1 = 0, beta2 = 0); site-2 beta = 0 alone gives 16 (site 1 generic or vacuum or gamma = 0 or conics), site-1 beta = 0 alone 21; **[3,1,0]: 40** at (alpha1 = 0, beta2 = 0); alpha1 = 0 alone 48, site-2 beta = 0 alone 48, site-2 alpha = 0 or b3 = 0 alone 50, everything else 54. The coincidence loci of Task 4 (w1' = w1 with w2' -> infinity: 10 / 21; with both w2 -> infinity: 8 / 14) are cheaper than any pair of independent simple loci; CG-completeness of these loci is not tested here (that is the reach test of Stage D).",
