   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Driver result — z-independence, (h, theta)-dependence, R -> 1 (the driver cell above; both reps)\n\nEach row rebuilds the setup, K tensor, R-matrix and the dressed locus analysis from this notebook's own file with the listed parameter line. Columns: Kt identical to the base one (exact, z-test points only), # support states of the nu1 = 1 slice, dimension of the R solution space, the conic constants of the dressed locus and cc1(-t) = (t+3)/(2(t+2)) (membership), the dressed count at a point of each conic, the per-label count of the dressed / undressed generic covector, sum P of the generic pair / the vacuum / Omega_c[w] (x) Omega_c[w'], max |R - 1|.\n\n| point | t | Kt identical | R dim | cc1(-t) in the conic constants | dressed gen / undressed gen | sum P (generic, vacuum, d) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **[2,1,0]** base | 62/35 | - | 1 | 167/264 = cc1(-t): True | 5 / 17 | 23, 18, 22 |\n| z' = (3/2,5/4,3/7) | 62/35 | **True** | 1 | True | 5 / 17 | 23, 18, 22 |\n| z'' = (2,5/4,2/3) | 62/35 | **True** | 1 | True | 5 / 17 | 23, 18, 22 |\n| h=1/3, theta=(1/5,-4/9) | 29/15 | - | 1 | 37/59 = cc1(-t): True | 5 / 17 | 23, 18, 22 |\n| h=1/2, theta=(3/7,-1/4) | 19/14 | - | 1 | 61/94: True | 5 / 17 | 23, 18, 22 |\n| theta2 = -100 | 1404/7 | - | 1 | 1425/2836: True | 5 / 17 | 23, 18, 22 |\n| **[3,1,0]** base | 62/35 | - | 1 | True (constants 1, 404/501, 167/264, 3371/7348, 101/66) | 7 / 40 | 54, 40, 54 |\n| z' | 62/35 | **True** | 1 | True | 7 / 40 | 54, 40, 54 |\n| z'' | 62/35 | **True** | 1 | True | 7 / 40 | 54, 40, 54 |\n| h=1/3, theta=(1/5,-4/9) | 29/15 | - | 1 | True (1, 89/111, 37/59, 2963/6549, 89/59) | 7 / 40 | 54, 40, 54 |\n| h=1/2, theta=(3/7,-1/4) | 19/14 | - | 1 | True (1, 50/61, 61/94, 1371/2867, 75/47) | 7 / 40 | 54, 40, 54 |\n| theta2 = -100 | 1404/7 | - | 1 | True | 7 / 40 | 54, 40, 54 |\n\n* **K is z-independent exactly for both reps** (the base Kt and the Kt at z' and z'' are identical sparse rational arrays).\n* The mirror reading holds at every (h, theta) tested: the dressed conic constant of the adjoint is cc1(-t) = (t+3)/(2(t+2)) (it is also among the [3,1,0] constants, together with cc = 1 = the vacuum family, which gives the best [3,1,0] count 5); the R solution space is 1-dimensional; the counts (23, 18, 22 resp. 54, 40, 54 for the generic pair, the vacuum and Omega_c[w] (x) Omega_c[w']) do not depend on (h, theta, z) at the tested points.\n* R -> 1: max |R - 1| = 0.86 / 1.02 at t = 62/35 and 0.020 / 0.044 at t = 1404/7 (the entries of R - 1 are O(1/t)).\n* Times: [2,1,0] 1.4 s per point (8.7 s total); [3,1,0] 17-35 s per point (124 s total).",
