   "value": "### two-site rotation brackets (Stage B) — result (2026-10-11)\n\n**Setting.** gl(3), L = 2, companion frame, h = 1/2, theta = (2/7,-3/5) (t = 62/35), z = (3/2,5/4,2/3), w = (5/2,7/3,3/5), w' = (7/4,-2/5,9/7); [2,1,0] (64 states) and [3,1,0] (225 states); everything exact except the eigenstates/Q's/SoV covectors (prec 60, all identities 1e-39 or better). Notebook state: written as JSON; the cells were not executed natively (no controller / `wolfbook_runCell` answers 'NOT executed' on a freshly created file); every code cell was evaluated in the shared kernel K1 from exactly its saved source and the printed results are in the markdown cells below the code cells; the driver re-reads this file and wipes Global`.\n\n**1. K tensor (Task 1).** Kt is a 64 x 64 / 225 x 225 exact rational array, expansion error 1e-89 / 1e-150, rationalisation error 3e-74 / 4e-73, denominators <= 8 / 12 digits, **sparse (278 of 4096 / 2051 of 50625 nonzeros)**, full rank. The slice nu2 = 1 reproduces the one-site site-1 maps Kg[c2] (independent recomputation, exact), the slice nu1 = 1 Stage A's site-2 maps Kh[x1] (exact; 35 / 103 support states, 15 / 29 with x1 in F1). **z-independent exactly** (identical at z', z''); rational in t (rebuilt at three (h,theta)).\n\n**2. Supports (Task 2).** Every c1 (x) c2 with generic factors, and Omega_c[w] (x) Omega_c[w'] (and w = w'), has the FULL support (64 / 225 pairs, every block fully populated: slots 25,15,15,9 / 81,54,54,36); no dependence of the x1-set on x2. One-site limits reproduce the one-site supports (c1 (x) e1: 12 / 24 states, only site-2 labels (lambda1|lambda1 c2); e1 (x) c2: 35 / 103, triangular). The support is NOT the union of the one-site supports (it contains it and is everything).\n\n**3. R-matrix (Task 2b): the reading of the asymmetry is confirmed.** R exists, 1-dimensional solution space for both reps, R T_ab = Ttilde_ab R (9 entries, u-independent), ttilde_a R = R t_a, Btilde R = R B, R commutes with rho(g) (x) rho(g), (e1 (x) e1) R = e1 (x) e1, R -> 1 at large theta12 (all exact checks True). The correct dressing is **Phi = (e1 (x) c2) R** (not R^-1): support only on x1 in F1 (12 / 24 states), per-label count **5 / 7 generic** (undressed 17 / 40), conic locus with constant **cc = 167/264 = cc1(-t) = (t+3)/(2(t+2))** at t = 62/35 for the adjoint (count 4; also at (1/3,(1/5,-4/9)): 37/59, (1/2,(3/7,-1/4)): 61/94; the spec's 229/342 is not (t+3)/(2(t+2)), the formula is what is confirmed), and for [3,1,0] the best locus is the vacuum family beta + alpha gamma = alpha^2 (cc = 1) with count 5. Dressing the cheap site-1 rotation makes it expensive (17 / 40).\n\n**4. Block ranks and counts (Task 3; lower bound sum r / upper bound sum P, blocks (0,0),(0,1),(1,0),(1,1)):**\n\n| Phi | [2,1,0] r; sum r | P; sum P | [3,1,0] r; sum r | P; sum P |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| (a) generic pair | 5,3,3,3; 14 | 10,5,5,3; **23** | 9,6,6,6; 27 | 18,12,12,12; **54** |\n| (b) random covectors | same as (a) | 23 | same as (a) | 54 |\n| (c) Omega_c[w] x Omega_c[w] | 5,3,3,2; 13 | 10,3,3,2; **18** | 8,6,6,6; 26 | 22,6,6,6; **40** |\n| (d) Omega_c[w] x Omega_c[w'] (and reverse) | 5,3,3,2; 13 | 10,5,5,2; **22** | 9,6,6,6; 27 | 18,12,12,12; **54** |\n| (e) Omega_c[w] x e1 | 1,1,1,1; 4 | 1,2,1,1; 5 | 1,1,1,1; 4 | 1,2,1,1; **5** |\n| (e') e1 x Omega_c[w'] | 3,3,3,2; 11 | 5,4,4,2; 15 | 6,6,6,4; 22 | 10,9,9,7; 35 |\n| (f) c1(g1) x e1 | 1,1,1,1; 4 | 1,2,1,1; 5 | 1,1,1,1; 4 | 2,2,1,2; 7 |\n| (g) (e1 x Omega_c[w']) R | 1,1,1,1; 4 | 1,1,2,1; 5 | 1,1,1,1; 4 | 1,1,2,1; 5 |\n| (h) R-dressed two-rotation candidates | 5,3,3,3; 14 | **23** | 9,6,6,6; 27 | **54** |\n\nRegression: blocks of (e), (f) have rank <= 1 and P(c,c') = the one-site column 2-form half-ranks (checked); (f') reproduces Stage A (11 / 15, 22 / 35). Identities (phi-form and block form with explicit bracket products, all states) hold at 1e-39 or better for every Phi.\n\n**5. det6 regression.** Omega_c[w] (x) Omega_c[w] = det6[F_vac,w]/Psi_Q on all states, 1e-46..1e-44 / 1e-43..1e-40 (both w, w'); Psi_Q = M1_vac M2_vac. Expected structure: Laplace expansion of the single det6 = 20 terms (3x3 minor x complementary 3x3 minor), each block has r <= min(20, nMin) = nMin (non-binding) and the four blocks share the same 20 terms. Actual: vacuum block ranks (5,3,3,2) / (8,6,6,6) versus generic (5,3,3,3) / (9,6,6,6): lower (sum 13 vs 14, 26 vs 27), counts 18 vs 23 and 40 vs 54, and rank of phi 8 (full) / **12 (< 15)**. Nothing had to be fixed. (The relation 'sum r over blocks <= number of Laplace terms' is not a valid bound: sum r = 26 > 20 for [3,1,0], each Laplace term feeds all four blocks.)\n\n**6. Decisive comparison.** Count of Omega_c[w] (x) Omega_c[w']: **22 ([2,1,0]) / 54 ([3,1,0])** = generic pair (23 / 54), above the vacuum (18 / 40), above the one-site products (best x best: 16 / 25; generic x generic dressed: 25 / 49; undressed: 75 / 175 — below only the undressed one). **Two different vacua do not decouple at the bracket level and are not cheaper than a generic pair for [3,1,0]; the R-dressed candidates (h) are exactly generic.**\n\n**7. The 4-parameter family (Task 4).** Polynomial blocks in (a1,s1,a2,s2) = (1/w1,1/w2,1/w1',1/w2'). Generic r = (5,3,3,2) / (9,6,6,6), sum P = 22 / 54 (all 40 random samples). Rank-drop hypersurface components: coordinate hyperplanes (a1, a2, s2) plus high-degree factors; [3,1,0] block (1,1) also t-dependent ratios (9 a1 = 44 a2, quadrics); none of the 'obvious' coincidences w1 = w1' etc. is a matrix-rank drop for [2,1,0]. Sub-family counts (sum P): w1' = w1: **18 / 40** (= the vacuum count; blocks (0,1),(1,0),(1,1) exact P = r); w2' -> infinity: 14 / 45; w1' = w1 with w2' -> infinity: **10 / 21**; w1' = w1 with w2, w2' -> infinity: **8 / 14 (exact, P = r)**; other coincidences (w2' = w2, w1' = w2, w2' = w1, w1 = w2, w1' = w2') leave the generic 22 / 54. Counts never equal a product of one-site counts.\n\n**7b. Task 4b (cell after Task 4): the (inf,inf) family with w1 != w1'** (gaussCov[{a,0,a}] x gaussCov[{a',0,a'}], the confirmed w2, w2' -> infinity limit of Omega_c; three pairs, identical numbers; identities 1e-39 or better): [2,1,0] r = 3,3,2,2 (sum 10), P = 4,4,2,2, **sum P = 12** (generic 23, vacuum 18); [3,1,0] r = 6,6,6,6 (sum 24), P = 12,12,9,12, **sum P = 45** (generic 54, vacuum 40; no block exact; not cheap, no wedge listing). Asymmetric orders: gaussCov x Omega_c[w'] 20 / 54, Omega_c[w] x gaussCov 14 / 45. Rank-drop loci on the (a,a') plane: a = a', a = 0, a' = 0 plus t-dependent ratio lines for [3,1,0] (details in the Task 4b result cell). The 8 / 14 of item 7 was the global rotation a = a' only.\n\n**8. One-site-fixed loci (Task 5).** (A) site 2 = Omega_c[w'], g1 free: the site-1 vacuum family and the adjoint quadric are NOT reducing loci (22 / 54 on them as for generic g1); the reducing loci are cross loci depending on w': alpha = 1/w1' (20 / 49), with the vacuum condition 18 / 40, and beta = 0 (20 / 54): the sites do not decouple. (B) site 1 = Omega_c[w], g2 free: the site-2 vacuum family is a genuine rank-drop locus of block (1,1) (22 / 54), b3 = 0 gives 22 / 50, **beta = 0 gives 16 / 48**, common-w1 plus vacuum 18 / 40. Type-pair scan over simple loci: minimum 14 ([2,1,0]: (beta1 = 0, beta2 = 0) or (alpha1 = 0, beta2 = 0)) and 40 ([3,1,0]: (alpha1 = 0, beta2 = 0)); CG-completeness untested.\n\n**9. Timings (s), [2,1,0] / [3,1,0].** Setup cells 1-6: 0.8 / 6.8; det6 regression (cell 8): 0.8 / 2.3; K tensor + slices: 0.2 / 1.3; tools: 0.1 / 1.1; R-matrix: 0.3-0.8 / 7.8; dressed test + locus: 0.2 / 0.2; Task 3 blocks: 1.6-2.7 / 11.7; Task 4: 5 / 20-50 (the rank-drop determinants dominate); Task 5: 4-9 / 18-44 (drop loci); all cells except the driver ~ 10-15 s / ~ 70-130 s; driver 8.7 / 124 s.\n\n**10. Surprises.** (i) The count upper bound P is pivot-dependent and not monotone in r (vacuum [3,1,0] block (0,0): r = 8 but P = 22; generic r = 9, P = 18): the lower bound r is the robust number; both are reported. (ii) Two distinct vacua are as expensive as a generic pair for [3,1,0], so the plan's success target (~ 25 for [3,1,0]) is not met by Omega_w (x) Omega_w' itself; the reductions come from coincidences (w1' = w1) and w2 -> infinity limits. (iii) The d1 x d1 coefficient matrix phi of the vacuum has rank 12 < 15 for [3,1,0] but full rank 8 for the adjoint. (iv) K is very sparse. (v) The commutant of gl(3) on V (x) V needs the quartic coupling invariants for the multiplicity-2 irreps (adjoint: 6 of 8 from words in C12, D12, D21).\n\n**11. Skipped.** Greedy / tensor-rank minimisation of P (not asked); the termwise comparison of the 20 Laplace terms with the blocks (the per-ladder 3x3 minors are not polynomials in the monomials without the Baxter relations; the state-by-state identity was checked instead); Groebner bases for the rank-drop ideals (minors too large; common factors of random determinants / sub-family tables used instead, [3,1,0] block (0,0) only through a random line section); [3,2,0]; the CG-reach test of any family (Stage D); HANDOFF.\n\n**12. Recommendation for Stage C (updated).** The (inf,inf) family with w1 != w1' is CG-complete (Stage D) but costs sum P = 12 for [2,1,0] (good: roughly half of the generic 23, lower bound 10, wedge decomposition printed) and 45 for [3,1,0] (only 17 % below the generic 54 and above the vacuum 40; lower bound 24, every block still needs rank-2 wedge pairs: P = 12,12,9,12 with r = 6 each). So for the adjoint start Stage C from it (blocks (1,0),(1,1) exact, three wedge-terms in (0,0),(0,1)); for [3,1,0] the cost is the decisive negative number: no family found is both CG-complete and near 25. The common-w1 family (18 / 40) and the line beta2 = 0 (16 / 48) were not tested for reach; the global-rotation line (8 / 14) is exact but is a global rotation.",
